<title>USA: Fitch chairman H. Russell Fraser to retire March 1.</title>
<headline>Fitch chairman H. Russell Fraser to retire March 1.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fitch Investors Service said Thursday its chairman of the board H. Russell Fraser, who took over the rating agency in 1989 and revived it, will retire March 1.</p>
<p>David J. Allen, a Fitch board member since 1989, will succeed Fraser as chairman. Stephen W. Joynt, president, will continue to manage the operations of the rating agency.  </p>
<p>Fraser said in a statement he plans to pursue other personal and business interests.</p>
<p>He retains a substantial equity interest in the company, according to Fitch.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
